module std where

-- and — short-circuit logical AND. (Boolean, Boolean) → Boolean.
--
-- The clause LHS is the bare `and` (id `std:and`). Phase 5b6 had to call it
-- `andFn` because the parser reserved `and`/`or`/`not` as operator keywords; the
-- word-operator de-reservation precursor (landed `5121c5b8`, ahead of FM-retire-9
-- 9a) made them ordinary idents, so the `…Fn` divergence + the std.ts
-- `f.id === "std-and:andFn"` extraction seam are both RETIRED. No `@codeName`.
--
-- Pure expression; mirrors the pre-Phase-5b6 inline JSON-Logic body
-- at engine/src/modules/std.ts:2378 (`{and: [{var: "a"}, {var: "b"}]}`),
-- which dispatched via the named-op key `and` to `applyOp`'s short-
-- circuit case branch in json-logic.ts.
--
-- Decomposed via if-lowering: `if a then b else False`. The post-flip
-- body lowers to `{if: [{var: "a"}, {var: "b"}, {construct: ["False"]}]}`
-- — canonical structural-form dispatch through `applyOp`'s `if` branch,
-- which evaluates ONLY the chosen branch. Lazy-semantics preserved:
-- `b` is only evaluated when `a` is true (verified pre-5b6 probe:
-- `and(false, {"/":[1,0]})` returns False without divide-by-zero).
--
-- If-lowering source-of-truth migration (5b5 piloted on min/max numeric
-- comparators; 5b6 extended to Boolean short-circuits). Disproves the 5b5
-- "lazy-arg semantics blocker" framing — short-circuit forms ARE portable via
-- if-lowering through `applyOp`'s structural-form case branch.

@label "And"
@description "Logical AND — true when both operands are truthy. Short-circuit via if-lowering (Phase 5b6): `b` is only evaluated when `a` is true."
@tags "boolean" "operator"
and : (a: Boolean) -> (b: Boolean) -> Boolean
and a b = if a then b else False
